{title: 386 - The Sacred Anthem}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #386 • }
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: Eb}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 386}
{meta: category Doctrines - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Eb]The sacred anthem slowly rang
[Gm/D]Across [Ab/C]the fields [Bb7]of [Eb]praise,
[Eb]When [Gm/D]earth's first [D7]Sabbath made [Gm/D]complete
[Eb]All creatures and [Fm]all [Bb]days.
[Gm]Walking [Cm]with [Fm]God, there,
[Fm/Ab]Woman and [Ab]man [Bb7/Ab]together [Eb/G]share
[Eb/G]The [Ab]blessed Sabbath mood;
[Bb7/Ab]And [Cm]in [Bb/D]that [Eb]green and [Ab]golden world
[Fm]Know [Gm]all [Ab]God's [Eb/Bb]works [Bb7]are [Eb]good.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Eb]But now in our [Ab/Eb]diminished [Eb]lives
[Gm/D]We [Ab/C]sing a blemished [Eb]song;
[Eb]The [Gm/D]earth is [D7]worn [Bb/D]and [D7]disarrayed
[Eb]And [Bb/F]all our [Eb]work [Fm]goes [Bb]wrong.
[Gm]Still [Fm/C]in [Cm]our [Fm]worship,
[Fm/Ab]Joining in [Ab]praise [Bb7/Ab]and [Gm]fellowship,
[Eb/G]By [Ab]Sabbath radiance [Bb7/Ab]blessed,
[Bb7/Ab]We [Cm]put [Bb/D]our [Eb]doubt and [Ab]fear away
[Fm]And [Gm]rest [Ab]within [Bb7]God's [Eb]rest.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[Eb]And arching [Ab/Eb]over time [Eb]and space
[Gm/D]The [Ab/C]Lord of Sabbaths [Eb]wills
[Eb]Renewal [D7]for [Bb/D]the [D7]weary [Dm]earth
[Eb]And [Bb/F]healing [Eb]for [Fm]our [Bb]ills.
[Gm]Hearts [Fm/C]will [Cm]rejoice [Fm]then;
[Fm/Ab]There will be [Ab]no [Bb7/Ab]more [Gm]weeping, [Eb/G]when
[Eb/G]We [Ab]know and shall be [Bb7/Ab]known.
[Bb7/Ab]With [Cm]hosts [Bb/D]of [Eb]the redeemed [Ab]we'll sing
[Fm]Around [Ab]God's [Eb/Bb]shining throne.
{end_of_verse}
